{"from": "claim:lk-11-49-51-abel-zechariah", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:zechariah-son-of-barachiah"}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-02", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-06-09", "note": "Luke's form is shorter: 'Father' alone in the earliest witnesses, without 'your will be done on earth as it is in heaven' and without the closing doxology; see the variants on Luke 11:2."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-09", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-07-07"}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-11", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-07-09", "note": "Both: bread vs stone; Luke adds fish vs snake and egg vs scorpion."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-15", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-24", "note": "Matthew: the Pharisees said it; Luke: some of the crowds."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-17", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-25", "note": "Luke 11:17-18 names Satan's kingdom explicitly."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-20", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-28", "note": "Luke: 'the finger of God' and 'kingdom of God'; Matthew: 'the Spirit of God' and 'kingdom of heaven'."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-29", "note": "Matthew: binding the strong man first; Luke: the strong man armed guarding his own dwelling."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-23", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-30"}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-24", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-43", "note": "Luke 11:24-26 adds the seven returning spirits more evil than the first."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-29", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-39", "note": "Matthew: 'an evil and adulterous generation'; Luke: 'an evil generation'."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-31", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-42"}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-32", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-41"}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-33", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-05-15", "note": "Matthew: a lamp under the measuring basket; Luke: in the cellar or under a basket."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-34", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-06-22", "note": "Matthew: 'if your eye is sound'; Luke: 'when your eye is good', with the warning of 11:35."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-39", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-23-25", "note": "Luke adds 'give for gifts to the needy those things which are within' (11:41)."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-43", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-23-06", "note": "Matthew adds salutations in the marketplaces and love of the chief seats at feasts; Luke addresses Pharisees only."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-47", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-23-29", "note": "Luke adds 'your fathers killed them' and the consent argument of 11:48."}
{"from": "passage:lk-11-54", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-12-14", "note": "Luke: scribes and Pharisees lie in wait to catch him in something he might say; Matthew: the Pharisees conspire to destroy him."}
{"from": "claim:lk-11-14-mute-demoniac", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-12-22-blind-mute-demoniac", "note": "Luke 11:14's demoniac is mute only; Matthew 12:22's is blind and mute."}
{"from": "claim:lk-11-16-sign-heaven", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-16-01-seek-sign", "note": "Luke 11:16: bystanders test him for a sign from heaven; Matthew 16:1: Pharisees and Sadducees ask for one."}
{"from": "claim:lk-11-30-jonah-sign", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-12-39-sign-of-jonah", "note": "Luke 11:30 says Jonah himself became a sign to the Ninevites; Matthew 12:40 spells out three days and three nights in the belly of the great fish."}
{"from": "claim:lk-11-37-38-handwashing", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-15-02-handwashing-before-eating", "note": "Luke 11:38: washing before dinner at a Pharisee's table; Matthew 15:2: disciples eating bread with unwashed hands."}
{"from": "claim:lk-11-42-tithe-herbs", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-23-23-tithing-herbs", "note": "Luke lists mint and rue and every herb; Matthew lists mint, dill and cumin."}
{"from": "claim:lk-11-44-hidden-graves", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-23-27-28-whitewashed-tombs", "note": "Luke's image is unmarked graves walked over unknowingly; Matthew's is whitewashed tombs that are visible."}
{"from": "claim:lk-11-49-51-abel-zechariah", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-23-35-zechariah-killed", "note": "Luke names no father for Zechariah and reverses the phrase to 'between the altar and the sanctuary'; Matthew names Zechariah son of Barachiah."}
{"from": "text:2-chronicles-24-20-21", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:lk-11-49-51-abel-zechariah", "note": "2 Chronicles 24:20-21: Zechariah son of Jehoiada the priest was stoned in the court of the LORD's house - the martyrdom usually identified with Luke's Zechariah; the identification is disputed, and Luke names no father."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-yadayim-2-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-11-37-38-handwashing", "grade": "B", "note": "Mishnah Yadayim 2:1 rules on hands made clean by poured water - the tractate of ritual handwashing behind the expectation; redacted c. 200 CE. Regraded C to B per the architect's Mishnah ruling (2026-11-15): the Mishnah names the same practice the claim states."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-maasrot-4-5", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-11-42-tithe-herbs", "grade": "B", "note": "Maasrot 4:5 rules garden herbs must be tithed; redacted c. 200 CE. It names dill, not rue: it attests the practice, not Luke's list. Regraded C to B per the architect's Mishnah ruling (2026-11-15): the Mishnah names the same practice the claim states."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-shekalim-1-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-11-44-hidden-graves", "grade": "C", "note": "Shekalim 1:1: the court marks gravesites so people can avoid impurity - the marking presupposed by 'hidden' unmarked graves; redacted c. 200 CE."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-avot-1-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-11-45-46-lawyers-burdens", "grade": "C", "note": "Avot 1:1: the Men of the Great Assembly said 'make a fence round the Torah' - the multiplying of restrictions the woe attacks; redacted c. 200 CE and about an ideal, not the lawyers' practice."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-avot-1-1", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:sefaria-avot-1-1"}
